      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 14,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "id": "tHpO8vy5TpARI1zh",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 800,
      "width": 1080,
      "height": 162.5,
      "text": "Key design points\n\u2022 FIFO is implicit: available_since timestamp orders engineers; escalation_queue.order_key orders waiting customers \u2014 no extra list bookkeeping.\n\u2022 Every state transition (Escalate / SetPresence / Completed / Decline) runs as ONE Postgres transaction (Router.withTx), so concurrent requests\n  from multiple csm-portal/backend instances can never double-assign the same engineer or the same queued case.\n\u2022 Going Offline mid-session doesn't drop the customer: pending_offline is set, engineer stays BUSY until Completed(), then flips to OFFLINE\n  and does NOT rejoin the pool or take a queued case.\n\u2022 Dismissing an alert (Decline) re-routes the case to another available engineer, or re-queues it at the FRONT (the customer already waited once).\n\u2022 Resilience: if chat-routing-service is down, csm-portal/backend falls back to the old broadcast-to-all-engineers SSE key so escalations still land.\n\u2022 chat-routing-service owns its own database (chat_routing) \u2014 separate from entity-service's own Postgres DB (db) and its flat 'cases' table;\n  the two schemas never mix.",
      "originalText": "Key design points\n\u2022 FIFO is implicit: available_since timestamp orders engineers; escalation_queue.order_key orders waiting customers \u2014 no extra list bookkeeping.\n\u2022 Every state transition (Escalate / SetPresence / Completed / Decline) runs as ONE Postgres transaction (Router.withTx), so concurrent requests\n  from multiple csm-portal/backend instances can never double-assign the same engineer or the same queued case.\n\u2022 Going Offline mid-session doesn't drop the customer: pending_offline is set, engineer stays BUSY until Completed(), then flips to OFFLINE\n  and does NOT rejoin the pool or take a queued case.\n\u2022 Dismissing an alert (Decline) re-routes the case to another available engineer, or re-queues it at the FRONT (the customer already waited once).\n\u2022 Resilience: if chat-routing-service is down, csm-portal/backend falls back to the old broadcast-to-all-engineers SSE key so escalations still land.\n\u2022 chat-routing-service owns its own database (chat_routing) \u2014 separate from entity-service's own Postgres DB (db) and its flat 'cases' table;\n  the two schemas never mix.",
      "seed": 1102847265,
      "versionNonce": 911241476,
      "version": 1
    }
